    skos:altLabel "antigen-binding groove"@en ;
    skos:definition """1) Pocket in a major histocompatibility complex (MHC) molecule that binds antigen for antigen presentation.
2) Hydrophobic binding region in the CD1 protein that anchors lipid-containing antigens causing exposure of the peptide or carbohydrate moiety in a position enabling T-cell receptor (TCR) contact."""@en ;
